INT. CHEESE CAVE - NIGHT

A cold limestone tunnel lined with racks of wheeled cheese. Condensation drips. A single bulb. Behind a rack, a ventilation grate half-pried loose.

ZOFIA LAWNICZAK, 30s, black clothes, headlamp, crouches at the grate with a screwdriver. A dark rectangle of vault door gleams behind it.

She sets down the screwdriver. Pulls a small recorder from her pocket. Presses play.

ZOFIA (V.O.)
(recording, her own voice)
Zofia, if you're hearing this, the guard rotates at two. The grate is the third rack from the end. Do not use the main door.

She clicks it off. Frowns. Looks at the rack. Counts.

ZOFIA
(muttering)
One. Two. Three.

She presses play again.

ZOFIA (V.O.)
(recording)
The vault has a thumbprint scanner. I have the thumb. It is in the Brie.

Zofia's eyes widen. She turns to the nearest wheel. Cuts into it with a pocketknife. Cheese falls away.

Inside: a small plastic bag. Inside the bag, a rubber thumb. She holds it up in the beam of her headlamp.

ZOFIA (CONT'D)
(whispering)
You are insane.

She presses play a third time.

ZOFIA (V.O.)
(recording)
Yes. Now hurry. Somewhere above you, he is awake.

Zofia freezes. Overhead, a footstep, then another. A beam of light sweeps the tunnel.

She switches off her headlamp. Everything goes black.

ZOFIA
(barely audible)
Fine. Fine.

She presses the thumb against the scanner. Click. The vault door sighs open.
